WEBVTT

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.840
This is a book you don't just

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.440
read,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.350
you do it.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.430
Each chapter is an exercise,

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:11.810
not an explanation.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:12.620
10 of them.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:13.850
You open a terminal,

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:14.620
you type,

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:15.600
you watch what happens,

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.320
and by the end you've built real

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:18.000
things,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.200
on real servers,

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.560
with an AI agent working beside you.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.310
You don't need to be a programmer,

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.680
you just need to be willing to

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.530
try.

00:00:25.944 --> 00:00:28.064
Exercise 1 sets up your workshop,

00:00:28.064 --> 00:00:28.924
a terminal,

00:00:28.924 --> 00:00:30.084
a package manager,

00:00:30.084 --> 00:00:30.684
git,

00:00:30.684 --> 00:00:32.174
the GitHub command line,

00:00:32.184 --> 00:00:33.514
and an AI assistant.

00:00:33.664 --> 00:00:36.324
Exercise 2 sends your first pull request.

00:00:36.324 --> 00:00:37.824
You fork a real book,

00:00:37.824 --> 00:00:39.404
write a review of one chapter,

00:00:39.404 --> 00:00:40.784
and propose it on GitHub,

00:00:40.784 --> 00:00:42.724
where real people will read it.

00:00:42.724 --> 00:00:44.414
This isn't a simulation.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.500
Then you start building.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.480
Take an open source presentation,

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.560
describe your topic in plain English,

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.010
and let the agent generate the pictures,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.470
the narration and the animated background.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:56.380
Next,

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.280
pair program a travel bucket list app

00:00:58.280 --> 00:00:59.200
from scratch.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.280
You describe it,

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.920
the agent writes every line,

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:02.870
and you review,

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:03.740
click around,

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:04.770
and ask for better.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.190
You bring the vision.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:07.710
The agent brings the code.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:10.300
Your app works on your own laptop.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.070
Now send the link to a friend.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:12.950
You can't.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.530
So you rent a small server,

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:16.070
and the agent runs it for you.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.150
It logs in,

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:18.200
locks the doors,

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.050
turns on HTTPS,

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:21.490
and points your domain at it.

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:23.170
Then you attack your own app before

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:24.310
anyone else does.

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:26.650
A team of security agents probes it,

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:27.910
tries real exploits,

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:29.260
and writes you a report.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.156
Change one thing,

00:01:31.156 --> 00:01:32.906
and how do you know nothing broke?

00:01:32.936 --> 00:01:34.106
Without tests,

00:01:34.176 --> 00:01:36.216
your agent is coding blindfolded.

00:01:36.216 --> 00:01:37.896
So you give it eyes:

00:01:37.896 --> 00:01:39.936
tests that go green when everything works,

00:01:39.936 --> 00:01:41.476
and red when it doesn't,

00:01:41.476 --> 00:01:42.756
on every push.

00:01:42.756 --> 00:01:44.296
Then you step out of the loop,

00:01:44.296 --> 00:01:46.176
and wire up a pipeline of agents

00:01:46.176 --> 00:01:47.826
that reads messy feedback,

00:01:47.996 --> 00:01:48.556
sorts it,

00:01:48.556 --> 00:01:50.486
and files the issues while you sleep.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.360
Exercise nine is the real thing.

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:54.430
Your own product,

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:56.260
from idea to launch in a day.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:57.250
Sign up,

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:57.990
log in,

00:01:57.990 --> 00:01:58.670
payments,

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.680
a smart A I feature,

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:00.810
tests,

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.370
and a live address you can text

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:03.390
to a friend.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.780
The agent is your co-founder.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:07.330
Every skill from every chapter comes together

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:08.180
here.

00:02:08.582 --> 00:02:10.942
And the last exercise turns the book

00:02:10.942 --> 00:02:11.562
around.

00:02:11.562 --> 00:02:12.992
For nine chapters,

00:02:13.022 --> 00:02:14.532
you followed instructions.

00:02:14.642 --> 00:02:15.912
Now you write them.

00:02:15.942 --> 00:02:18.482
A claw .md file that tells an

00:02:18.482 --> 00:02:19.882
agent how to work on your project,

00:02:19.882 --> 00:02:20.922
what matters,

00:02:20.922 --> 00:02:22.242
and what not to touch.

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.982
You walked in as a passenger.

00:02:23.982 --> 00:02:25.532
You leave as the captain.

00:02:25.562 --> 00:02:27.612
Open a terminal and start.
